<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balfour Declaration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balfour Declaration was a public statement issued by the British government on 2 November 1917, in a letter from Foreign Secretary Arthur Balfour to Lord Rothschild, supporting 'a national home for the Jewish people' in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>. It also stated that the rights of existing non-Jewish communities should not be prejudiced. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> incorporated it into the Mandate for Palestine in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balfour-declaration.jpg" alt="Balfour Declaration" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United Kingdom Government signed by Arthur Balfour · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balfour_declaration_unmarked.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
